  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   The central idea is to refine and optimize the existing coordinate descent and local search methods by incorporating population-based global search techniques to escape local optima. The current algorithm may be prone to isolated local minima due to its step-by-step refinement. This approach will enhance exploration by combining phase-based optimization with random restarts, guided by exponential cooling schedules. This strategy addresses the problem's non-convexity and aims to improve the upper bound of Erd\u0151s discrepancy constant C by finding better global minima. While the approach builds upon existing methods, it introduces randomness in restarts and adaptive cooling to explore diverse configurations.\n\n 2. Mathematical specification\n   The optimization is performed over a discrete step function h of length n, with constraints:\n     - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n     - sum(h) = n/2 exactly\n   The objective is to minimize:\n     C_5 = max_k \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx\n   Discrete evaluation: normalize the full correlation of h and (1-h) by dx=2/n.\n\n   Phase-based optimization:\n     - Phase A: **Aggressive coordinated descent** with increased grid resolution (max_passes=1000) and higher penalty (50) to enforce constraints.\n     - Phase B: **Smooth optimization** using alpha-exponential barrier (alpha=500000) to smooth the objective while preserving variance.\n     - Phase C: **Pair-wise search** with varying radii (40) and step sizes (0.01, 0.005, 0.001) to explore pairwise adjustments.\n     - Phase D: **Re-weighted SLSQP** with adaptive alpha parameterization and bounds management.\n\n   Key hyperparameters:\n     - Random seed for reproducbility\n     - Multi-phase budget allocation (35% to initial descent, 25% to polishing)\n     - Minimal restart frequency (every 200 seconds)\n     - Cooling schedule based on elapsed time\n\n 3. Implementation procedure\n   Stage 1: Initialize parent solution\n     - Represent parent as n-point sample\n     - Project to [0,1] with exact sum (n/2) via iterative clipping and redistribution\n\n   Stage 2: Global optimization loop\n     for each optimization phase with budget update:\n        - Phase A (time-weighted budget):\n          * Run agressive coordinate descent:\n            - For passes = 1 to 1000:\n              \u2022 Use grid size 120\n              \u2022 Track 1-level change along coordinate directions\n          * Post-process with projection\n\n        - Phase B (time-weighted budget):\n          * Use alpha-SLSQP with bounds [0,1] and equality constraint\n          * Obonjective: float(np.max(compute_corr(h, n)) * (2.0/n)\n\n        - Phase C (time-allocated cooling schedule):\n          * When time passes 400s, reduce alpha by factor 0.9 and continue SLSQP\n\n   Stage 3: Restart strategy\n     for each restart every 200s:\n        \u2022 Scale noise level sqrt(max(1, log(1/ratio)))\n        \u2022 Sample from normal distribution with mean=current best, std=noise\n        \u2022 Project to feasible space and re-add multiset\n\n   Stage 4: Termination conditions\n     - Track best_c found during all phases\n     - Check time budget (1100s max)\n     - Return best candidate (h, rounded_nested_c) that satisfies:\n        0 <= h[i] <= 1 for all i\n        sum(h) = n/2 exactly\n\n 4. Search choices and variations\n   Default strategy:\n    - n_candidates = 2-10 dynamic based on time\n    - cooling_rate = 2.0 (# times worse threshold can get before cooling)\n    - restart_frequency = 200s\n\n   Adaptive variations:\n    - **Time-dependent alpha**: exponentially decay from 500000 to 50 every 200s\n    - **Radius-aware pair search**: focus attention within n/4 neighborhood\n    - **Nest-level refinement**: alternate between low-runs (pair-wise) to high-runs (full-length)\n\n   Triggered variations:\n     - If best_c improves by <0.0001, activate temperature drops\n     - If time remaining <120s, switch to exhaustive neighborhood search\n     - Remove any candidate deviating by >2sd from mean value\n\n 5. Budget allocation\n   Total time: 1100s\n   - Phase A: 400s (initiation)\n   - Phase B: 400s (SLSQP polishing)\n   - Cooling phases: distributed over 300s\n   - Restart windows: every 200s for up to 2 restarts\n   - Final pass: verification and cleaning\n\n 6. Validation checks\n   - Ensure final candidate satisfies sum(h) = n/2\n   - Compute c5 using exact np.correlate(..., mode='full')\n   - Time-based budget check:\n        if t_current > deadline: return best found\n   - Noise threshold check for restarts:\n        |log(cand) - best| <= time_remaining * 0.001",
